short_label: X.91
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and a first apotome, then the side of the area is an apotome.
----
proof:

Let the area *AB* be contained by the rational straight line *AC* and the first apotome *AD*.

I say that the side of the area *AB* is an apotome.

